Subject: [PATCH] media: uapi: add MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SENSOR_DATA

The backported Raspberry Pi IMX708 driver uses MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SENSOR_DATA
for the sensor's embedded-data (ancillary metadata) stream. That symbol
only exists in the Raspberry Pi kernel tree.

Signed-off-by: Marcin Bober <mbober1@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate
---
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h b/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
--- a/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
@@ -179,7 +179,12 @@
  * metadata format that is not configurable from userspace.
  * Width and height will be set to 0 for this format.
  */
 #define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_METADATA_FIXED		0x7001
 
+/*
+ * Sensor ancillary metadata formats - next is 0x7002
+ */
+#define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SENSOR_DATA		0x7002
+
 /* Generic line based metadata formats for serial buses. Next is 0x8008. */
 #define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_META_8			0x8001
